[Music]  we were able to work on this project  with multiple government stakeholders to  come up with a new prototype  to bring the kung pong spirit which  celebrates healthy communal living  into the urban setting of singapore the  overarching theme of this project is  connection  and integration it is a new prototype of  mixed use which combines public housing  for the elderly  republic space and park medical health  and recreational amenities  retail shops food centre and an urban  farm  the first challenge we faced was how to  accommodate all the facilities on this  very small site  our design approach is to layer these  different programs vertically  so there are three layers the lowest  layer is the ground layer with  supermarket retail shops and food center  and by  compacting this commercial footprint we  freed the ground floor  for a tropical plaza and by lifting the  medical center to the middle layer  we can have all the weather activities  in a fully public  porous and pedestrianized plaza below  the upper level  is for community users of a quieter  nature  such as the child care elder care and  elderly housing apartments  over all these uses we created a new  elevated ground level by introducing  a community sky garden where young and  all can come together  so instead of standalone programs we  have created  a layered more integrated urban village  with all these mixed uses  and its tropical community spaces  our approach in kampung mrot is  three-dimensional programming  multiplying and maximizing the building  systems of greenery and community spaces  making both systems useful and enjoyable  the integrated design of compound  emerity and the extensive programming by  all the various stakeholders have  actually helped to encourage  our senior residents to get out of their  flats  socialize with their neighbours and  pursue their interests  you

